        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the following quantities:\n- In Sam's first 100 matches, he won 50%.\n- In his next 100 matches, he won 60%.\n\nThe unknown I needed to find was the total number of matches Sam won.\n\nTo solve this, I first calculated the number of matches won in the first 100 games. Since he won 50% of them, I used the operation:\n\\[ 100 \\times 0.50 = 50 \\]\nThis calculation was based on the given percentage and the number of matches. I expected this to give me the number of matches won in the first set of games.\n\nNext, I calculated the number of matches won in the next 100 games. Using the given 60%:\n\\[ 100 \\times 0.60 = 60 \\]\nThis operation was straightforward and directly applied the percentage to the number of matches.\n\nTo find the total number of matches won, I added the two results:\n\\[ 50 + 60 = 110 \\]\nThis addition combined the matches won from both sets of games.\n\nTo check the result, I verified that the operations were correctly applied and the arithmetic was accurate. The final number, 110, represented the total number of matches Sam won.\n\nThe operations I used were straightforward percentage calculations and addition, which I would reuse in similar problems involving percentages and totals.\n\nFINAL: 110",
