        "target": "Given:\n- Isabela bought 100 cucumbers.\n- She bought twice as many cucumbers as pencils, so she bought 100 / 2 = 50 pencils.\n- Both cucumbers and pencils cost $20 each.\n- She got a 20% discount on the pencils.\n\nFirst, calculate the cost of the cucumbers:\n- Cost of 100 cucumbers = 100 * $20 = $2000.\n\nNext, calculate the cost of the pencils before the discount:\n- Cost of 50 pencils = 50 * $20 = $1000.\n\nNow, apply the 20% discount to the pencils:\n- Discount on pencils = 20% of $1000 = 0.20 * $1000 = $200.\n- Cost of pencils after discount = $1000 - $200 = $800.\n\nFinally, add the cost of the cucumbers and the discounted pencils:\n- Total cost = $2000 (cucumbers) + $800 (pencils) = $2800.\n\nFINAL: 2800",
